{
  "note": "Nineteen shots from six archive photographs and one silent newsreel. Each photograph plays wide and then pushed in; the newsreel is spread across four short bursts rather than played once, because a page of stills reads as a slideshow after fifteen seconds and men swinging axes at barrels reset the eye without changing the subject. The footage is letterboxed at exactly the geometry the photographic bands use — same width, same centre — so it sits inside the cut instead of interrupting it. No end card. The one dark beat in the middle is deliberate: the seven hundred deaths land on black, because there is no photograph of them and pretending otherwise would be the one dishonest frame in the film.",
